    },
    {
      "id": "df7b6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Although completion of the coursework listed below is not mandatory prior to admission, students are advised to complete as much lower-division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. Additional Resources: See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. Visit our Sac State Apply page for more information about our campus! Visit the Admissions website for current transfer admission requirements. Connect with an Admissions Counselor .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(29, 32, 36); font-size: 14px;\">Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! </strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Although completion of the coursework listed below is not mandatory prior to admission, students are advised to complete as much lower-division course preparation as possible prior to transfer. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Additional Resources:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.csus.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>University Catalog</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit our </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Sac State Apply</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> page for more information about our campus!</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit the </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/application-process/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions website</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for current transfer admission requirements. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Connect with an </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/connect-with-admissions.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions Counselor</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">. </span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "63796f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "MAJOR INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "67796f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Students must earn a minimum grade of \"C-\" or higher in all courses required in the major. Prior to acceptance as a Journalism major, students must first complete a pre-major consisting of all required lower-division courses plus JOUR 130A and JOUR 130B. Please note, JOUR 130A and JOUR 130B are upper-division courses and must be completed at Sacramento State. All pre-major courses must be completed with a \"C-\" grade or higher. Students with a Sacramento State grade point average of 2.30 or higher may request early admission to the major after transfer. Students may major either in Journalism or in Political Science-Journalism. For additional information on the combined program, please see the \"Political Science and Journalism, BA\" major articulation agreement. The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Journalism is compatible with the B.A. in Journalism at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better. Journalism majors are the core of students who write for The State Hornet , a weekly campus newspaper. For additional information, please visit: Department of Communication Studies .",
      "contentHtml": "<ol><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students must earn a minimum grade of \"C-\" or higher in all courses required in the major.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Prior to acceptance as a Journalism major, students must first complete a pre-major consisting of all required lower-division courses plus JOUR 130A and JOUR 130B. Please note, JOUR 130A and JOUR 130B are upper-division courses and must be completed at Sacramento State. All pre-major courses must be completed with a \"C-\" grade or higher. Students with a Sacramento State grade point average of 2.30 or higher may request early admission to the major after transfer.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students may major either in Journalism or in Political Science-Journalism. For additional information on the combined program, please see the \"Political Science and Journalism, BA\" major articulation agreement.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Journalism is compatible with the B.A. in Journalism at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Journalism majors are the core of students who write for </span><a href=\"https://statehornet.com/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>The State Hornet</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">, a weekly campus newspaper. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">For additional information, please visit: </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/college/arts-letters/communication-studies/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Department of Communication Studies</strong></a><strong style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</strong></li></ol>"
    }
  ],
